    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1953-p22.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The printed expression is a product of two separate radicals: \\[ 27\\sqrt[4]{9}\\sqrt[3]{9} =3^{3+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{3}}=3^{\\frac{25}{6}}. \\] Its base-\\(3\\) logarithm is \\(\\frac{25}{6}=4\\dfrac16.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite \\(27\\) and both occurrences of \\(9\\) as powers of \\(3\\)",
        "Add the exponents \\(3,\\) \\(\\frac{1}{2},\\) and \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
